30,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The minutes show no review in five years. The neighbor’s block had arrears and absenteeism from charges.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,The sticker register shows daily riders prefer paying over equal claims. Morning shifts are frequent.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,Four out of eleven morning departures required shifting bikes. The rain row is useless in winter.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The ledger is empty for capital. The station park is 2,600 yen with a waitlist.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,Billing takes three hours monthly. The double-tier rack needs greasing twice a year and is slow to use.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, if we charge, we risk the neighbor’s problem. But the station park is expensive.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, the shifting is a real issue. But do people want to pay?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, the rain makes half the spots bad. The shifting is a daily friction.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, the station park is a benchmark. 2,600 yen is high, but the waitlist shows demand.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the maintenance burden is real. Three hours a month is significant for one person.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,A lottery might avoid the payment friction. But it ignores the rain and shifting issues.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"Shared racks might solve the shifting, but the greasing and slow loading are problems.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The rain and shifting suggest we need better placement or a system that accounts for it.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"The financials suggest a small charge is feasible, but the maintenance cost is high.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The maintenance is the killer. Who does the greasing? Who reconciles the cash?,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I lean towards a lottery to avoid payment disputes, but we need to address the rain.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I think a small charge is fair, given the daily riders’ preference.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I support a system that reduces morning friction. Maybe a lottery with priority for dry spots?,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I support a paid allocation, but we need to automate the billing to reduce the three-hour burden.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I am concerned about the maintenance. If we choose paid, we need a clear plan for the greasing and reconciliation.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
